API and data flow
The page calls the MediaWiki API with action=query, format=json, prop=extracts|links, exintro=1, explaintext=1, pllimit=20, and plnamespace=0. The origin=* parameter supports cross-origin requests from a browser. The search term is URL-encoded before being sent. The response is parsed as JSON; the first returned page supplies the title, extract, and linked page titles. Those titles become graph nodes connected to the selected central topic.

This project does not contain a private API key, custom REST server, authentication service, or server-side database. The visible "Wikipedia API v2 Live" label is interface text; the code uses the Wikipedia MediaWiki API endpoint shown in the JavaScript.
